{
  "name": "Stripe card payments: gross charges, fees, and a net payout",
  "description": "Two customers pay their July invoices by card through Stripe: $49 and $99 monthly subscriptions. Each charge is collected at GROSS ($49.00, $99.00) into a financial account for the Stripe balance, which clears that invoice's receivable. Stripe is a vendor with its own contract: its fee on each charge (2.9% + 30 cents: $1.72 and $3.17, $4.89 in all) is an expense on 5230 payment processing paid out of the Stripe balance account, and the payout is a transfer_cash of the net ($143.11) from the Stripe balance account to the bank. The provider fee a payment method posts with a recorded payment applies to outbound pay effects only, so a card collection's fee is recorded here on the Stripe contract, once. After the payout the Stripe balance is zero, the bank holds $143.11, receivables are zero, 5230 holds $4.89, and July revenue is the gross $148.00.",
